.TH NULLFETCH 1 "2026-11-14" "nullfetch 1.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nullfetch \- tiny system fetch for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nullfetch
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nullfetch
prints system information next to an ASCII logo. It uses only the Python
standard library and needs no configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-logo
Hide the ASCII logo.
.TP
.BR \-\-logo " " \fINAME\fR
Show the given logo: \fIauto\fR (distribution logo), \fInone\fR, or a name
from \fBlogos.py\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-logo\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Use a custom ASCII art file.
.TP
.BR \-\-accent " " \fICOLOR\fR
Accent color in \fB#rrggbb\fR form.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colors.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Use ASCII-only bars, ellipsis and separators.
.TP
.BR \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Output width in columns.
.TP
.B \-\-oneline
Print one compact line for status bars.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-logos
List available logo names and exit.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-only " " \fIFIELDS\fR
Show only the given fields, comma separated.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print system information as JSON.
.SH FIELDS
user, host, os, kernel, cpu, gpu, ram, disk
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-only cpu,ram
Show only the CPU and RAM lines.
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-no\-logo \-\-json
Print JSON without a logo.
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-logo cat
Use the cat logo.
.TP
.B nullfetch \-\-oneline \-\-only ram,disk
One compact line with memory and disk usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colors when set to a non-empty value.
.SH LICENSE
MIT
